decoherence-24398131.conceptual_definition:
The formula 
$$P(\text{Reverse}) = P(\text{Forward}) e^{-\Delta S / k_B} 
$$ relates the probability of a process occurring in reverse, $P(\text{Reverse})$, to the probability of it occurring in the forward direction, $P(\text{Forward})$, and the change in entropy, $\Delta S$, of the system and its surroundings during the process. It highlights that processes with a significant increase in entropy are much more likely to occur in the forward direction than in reverse.
